+/*
+ * apklayer patch (0061): instructions of features the claimed CPU (berberis.cpuinfo profile pixel5: Kryo 475 Silver, a Cortex-A55-class ARMv8.2 core: no FCMA,
+ * JSCVT, FlagM, FRINT32/64, BF16, I8MM, SB, SSBS, DIT, PAuth, MTE, RNG, SHA3/SHA512/SM3/SM4, FHM, LRCPC2/3, LSE128, HBC, MOPS, CSSC, WFxT, DPB2) does not have, and the
+ * EL1-only system instructions, are UNDEFINED, as on that CPU (SIGILL): an anti-emulation probe executes them and expects the fault. Berberis can run most of them, but
+ * its HWCAP / cpuinfo / ID registers (patch 0010, the Mrs table) deny them, so executing them told translation from hardware. The table is (mask, value) over the
+ * instruction word, generated by assembling sample instructions with clang and keeping the bits that are constant across register/arrangement/size variants
+ * (tools/ace/genmask.py); it was checked against the .text of the arm64 Android libraries (only libcrypto's SHA512 and libstagefright's USDOT match: HWCAP-gated code).
+ * Knob berberis.isa_gate (env BERBERIS_ISA_GATE): "a76" turns the gate on; off (default) = the instruction runs as before.
+ */
